					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-05 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="text-decoration: underline" class="Apple-style-span">STK Tour Journal #1</span></span><div><span style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span></div><div>We&#39;re
4 hours into our road trip and are making a short stop in Portland. I&#39;m
feeling excited about heading down to the bay for show #1 and seeing
hella good folks, kasamas and allies. Our rental has a filthy GPS
system so we&#39;re lookin fwd to messin with that a little bit. My ears
have already been treated to the following:</div><div><br /></div><div>*Massline mixtape</div><div>*New beats for the Common Market LP</div><div>*Unmastered Blue Scholars&#39; Bayani LP</div><div><br /></div><div><span class="Apple-style-span">Thoughts? Upon first impression, the mixtape is like the 2007 version of the <span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">Do The Math Compilation</span>,
in where hella emcees are just doing their thing over consistent,
bangin beats. It&#39;s already a historic collab of ML artists and local
cats, some or most who inhabit the <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">ML forum</span>. Big up to everyone involved in this project!</span></div><div><br /></div><div>The Common Market beats are bangin&#39;! Big up Sabzi!</div><div><br /></div><div>The
Bayani album is gonna surprise everyone. It&#39;s a soup of all type of
different ingredients, and it sure tastes hella good. Check out the
info to your right about the Bayani release party.</div><div><br /></div><div>Looks like we gotta bounce. Big up to Claire (and her cat, Faith) for the hospitality!</div><div><br /></div><div><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">Excelcior!</span></div><div>daps</div><div><br /></div><div><br /></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-04 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br><span class="Apple-style-span">Geo here, live from a pitstop in Portland en route to San Francisco. DJ <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">daps1</span> and I have upgraded the rental car and I just had my first experience with a GPS navigation system. Sh*t is nuts! We&#39;re on the West Coast leg of the <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Stop the Killings Tour</span>, featuring myself and the comrade <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Kiwi</span> of <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Native Guns</span>. I&#39;ll be rocking new solo material off the upcoming <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Prometheus Brown</span> mixtape as well as classic <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Blue Scholars</span> joints and maybe even some previews off the new <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Bayani</span> album. Hold me down while I&#39;m gone from the 206 yall. And go and cop <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">GT&#39;s Lovework</span> album if you haven&#39;t already.</span><div><br /></div><div><div><span class="Apple-style-span"><div>For more info on the STK campaign and upcoming tour dates, go to http://www.cell68.com/stk</div><div><br /></div><div><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Sunday Mar 4	</span></span></div><div><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">w/ Kiwi, Denizen Kane &amp; Jern Eye<br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">Poeleng Lounge (21+)</span></div><div><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">San Francisco, CA </span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Tuesday Mar 6 </span></span></div><div><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">w/ Kiwi, The Committee &amp; guests<br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">The Promenade (21+) </span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">Long Beach, CA </span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Wednesday Mar 7 </span></span></div><div><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">w/ Kiwi, DJ Kuttin Kandi (5th Platoon), Dannu (of Visionaries) and Zanni De Jesus<br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">Che Cafe @ UCSD (All-Ages) </span></div><div><span style="border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">730PM | 0-10$ donation<br /></span><span style="border-collapse: collapse; -khtml-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -khtml-border-vertical-spacing: 2px; font-size: 12.1px" class="Apple-style-span">San Diego, CA </span></div><div>&nbsp;</div></span><br /></div></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-01 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><u><strong>cameos: word up!</strong></u><br /><br />like <strong>daps1</strong> keeps saying, us <strong>Massliners</strong> are everywhere.  these cameos were posted earlier in the forums, but i will share them now for any folks that are interested.<br /><br />this is a screenshot taken from the introductory video on the forthcoming <strong>Lebron James / Windows Vista</strong> promo website.  note the <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> poster in the upper left corner:<br /><br /><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/lebron.jpg" alt="" width="430" /><br /><br /><strong>Half Life 2</strong>, local game company <strong>VALVe</strong> <strong>Software</strong>&#39;s long awaited sequel to <strong>Half Life</strong> (the game that provided the engine for the world-famous <em>Counterstrike</em>) has a cameo on the CD player in <em>&quot;Dr. Kleiner&#39;s lab.&quot;</em>  look close and you can see what the doctor is listening to in the screenshot below:<br /><br /><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/bluevalve.jpg" alt="" width="430" /><br /><br />holler atcha &#39;Scholars with flics of any cameos or in-like-manner-filthy appearances of Massline-ness in yo&#39; section... <strong>IN THE FORUM</strong>.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-01 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><u><strong>this is why i&#39;m hot</strong></u><br /><br />the effects of <strong>global warming</strong> on our atmosphere are messin with a brovah&#39;s head right now.  i get on myspace and i see post after post from people who live about 15 minutes from me saying things like &quot;it&#39;s snowing outside!&quot; or &quot;we have 7 inches of snow!&quot;  <br /><br />then i look out the window and it&#39;s just sunny beacon hill to me.  oh hey there&#39;s the garbage truck... DAMN! i forgot to take the trash out again.<br /><br />but back to the subject at hand.  for today, i&#39;d just like to take a moment of silence to remember <br /><br /><br />


<a href="%22http://news.independent.co.uk/environment/article2099971.ece%22%3E%3Cb"><strong>Lohachara.</strong></a><br /><br /><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/lohachara.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br /><strong>Lohachara</strong> is an island off the coast of <strong>India</strong>--er, was.  the sea level has risen so much that a small island that used to be home to 10,000 indigenous people is now submerged.<br /><br />this is why i&#39;m hot.<br />this is why i&#39;m hot.<br />this is why, this is why,<br />this is why i&#39;m hot.<br /><br />the earth is gettin warm,<br /><strong>opinion? this is not</strong>.<br /><br />this is why, this is why,<br />this is why i&#39;m hot.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-28 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><u><strong>respect my fresh</strong></u><br /><br /><strong>khalil</strong> and i hit the block, flipped the work, and made it do watt it do yesterday.  <br /><br />for us that means <em>&quot;drove around and looked at clothes.&quot;</em>  yes, in this day and age, the crass materialistic behavior that is cultivated in the minds of the people by a neo-imperialist economic superstructure has led two doods each with a class consciousness--who also never really had money to spend on high-end gear--to get really into freshness manifest in cloth.  the art and design are just too filthy to ignore.<br /><br />you see, there&#39;s a reason i don&#39;t rap.<br /><br />at the recommendation of the homie <strong>Macklemore</strong>, one of the spots we hit up yesterday was a place called <strong>Sureel</strong> in <strong>Kirkland</strong>.  Kirkland (or as Khingz calls it, the &quot;K&quot;) is an interesting spot.  we can see the california-ization of washington state as certain things like clothes and live music--things that used to be only available in the city--are making their way out to the near-eastside suburbs.<br /><br /><img src="http://i85.photobucket.com/albums/k73/dougsureel/FASHION_SHOW_MARCH.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />if you live near Kirkland and you&#39;re into snowboarding, or just really want a <strong>$225 Greedy Genius hoodie</strong>, hit up the folkers at <a href="www.shopsureel.com"><strong>Sureel</strong></a>.<br /><br /><br /><u><strong>new music<br /></strong></u><br /><strong>Volume 1</strong> of the <strong>MASSLINE mixtape</strong> is almost finished.  not sure when we&#39;ll have it out, but rest assured, it&#39;ll see the light of day.<br /><br />it features MCs and beatmakers from all over the town including the <strong>MASSLINE artists</strong>, <strong>Khingz</strong>, <strong>Jerm</strong>, <strong>Asun</strong>, <strong>Hollis</strong>, <strong>Chev</strong>, <strong>Angel</strong>, <strong>Budo</strong>, <strong>Cin7</strong>, and many more.  as the homie <strong>Vitamin D</strong> said -- something about little time and too many songs to do -- we get approached by many folks from all over wanting to collab.  sometimes we don&#39;t have time, sometimes the schedules just don&#39;t fit, sometimes the music just wouldn&#39;t work for an album, and sometimes, the collabs would just be plain wack if we did them.  <br /><br />either way, many would say that these reasons are not good enough to keep people from hearing these tracks, so we decided to put together a mixtape.<br /><br /><strong>MASSLINE TV Volume 1</strong> is also in the works, scheduled for a release sometime this summer.  if you see us around the town with a camera, give us a holla!<br /><br />stay posted!<br /><br /><strong>saba</strong><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> [42] <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF